Task 2: Fixes #1163 (Kind: product). I filed #1163 during planning from today's real-wire capture.
• With no Gemini key set, yoyo sends the Anthropic key to Google (the documented fallback). Google answers 400 … API key not valid … API_KEY_INVALID. The error classifier only matches 401/"unauthorized"-style text, so the user sees raw JSON and the "set GEMINI_API_KEY" hint never prints.
• Test first, built from the captured body, asserting the full hint text. It includes a non-auth Google 400 that must not get the hint, and a check that the variable the hint tells the user to set is one yoyo actually reads.
• Other providers' bad-key replies are not added from memory; each one needs a vendor doc link or a captured response.

